  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Absolute bioavailability is 45% after a single 200 mg oral dose, and a high-fat meal changes exposure only slightly. Bound to plasma proteins at 96.3%, it is cleared mainly by hepatic metabolism.",
    "substance": "The active moiety has a molecular weight of 506.59 and is a white to yellow powder.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as tablets of 50, 100, 150 and 200 mg, taken twice daily.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning and no contraindications. Diarrhea and infections are among the most common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Adjuvant treatment of early breast cancer at high risk of recurrence, and advanced breast cancer, in hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative disease.",
    "mechanism": "Inhibits cyclin-dependent kinases 4 and 6, which blocks retinoblastoma protein phosphorylation and halts cell-cycle progression from G1 into S phase."
  },
  "tell": "A CDK4/6 inhibitor largely recovered in feces, about 81% of a dose, and dosed twice daily.",
